// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/tri/trigit/issue_hygiene_engine.t27 -- issue hygiene over the one canonical work graph: duplicates, stale
// issues, issues resolved elsewhere but still open, and the evidence a close or an archive needs (owner order
// T27V_ROADMAP_DASHBOARD_SYNC V3, 2026-11-08, Wave A: the contract).
//
// WHY. The board is honest only if the issue list is: a duplicate, a stale issue or an issue whose work already
// landed elsewhere makes the roadmap lie. This engine finds them from the graph and from recorded facts, never from
// text similarity, and it only RECOMMENDS a close: the close itself is owner-gated and needs evidence. Nothing is
// ever deleted -- an issue is closed, then archived (closed with the hygiene-review label removed).
//
// RULES:
//   duplicate         only through an outgoing DUPLICATES edge of the graph; a pair pointing at each other is a
//                     conflict for the owner, not a close
//   stale             no event, commit, PR or comment for 7 days (idle_ms, monotonic, t27os/t27t.t27); stale and
//                     no owner action for 14 days escalates: the hygiene-review label and owner_approval_required,
//                     never a priority change (priority is roadmap_dashboard_sync.t27's alone)
//   resolved-but-open a verified artifact or a SUPERSEDES edge (graph), a merged PR, passing tests
//   close evidence    an owner decision, or graph evidence (verified artifact or superseded) AND a merged PR AND
//                     passing tests; a duplicate's evidence is its DUPLICATES edge; every close is owner-gated
//   archive           an issue closed with evidence that still carries hygiene-review: the label sync removes it
//   run               daily (cron) or on demand, at most RD_CYCLE_MAX actions, the rest to the dead letter
//
// The engine writes nothing itself: it yields hygiene label bits (fed to rd_labels as RdLife.hygiene), events and
// recommendations; GitHub writes go through rd_write_allowed. This file imports roadmap_dashboard_sync.t27; that
// file never imports this one.
//
// NOT CLAIMED: no host, no cron and no GitHub call exist yet (Waves B..D); the tests were checked by hand, not run,
// because the swap gate was BLOCKED when this was written.

module TriTrigitIssueHygieneEngine;

